# Ketelhuis AR Unity Project

## Unity Version

Unity 6000.3.11f1

## Required Packages

* AR Foundation
* ARCore XR Plugin

## Project Overview

This project uses marker-based AR tracking.

When a tracked image is detected, an InteractionRoot prefab is spawned. The prefab contains two virtual valves. Valve values are sent to a Node.js server and can be visualized through a browser-based cabinet interface.

## Main Scripts

MarkerSpawnManager

Handles tracked image detection and spawns the InteractionRoot prefab.

WheelDragRotate

Handles valve interaction and stores ValveValue.

PressureSyncSender

Reads valve values and sends them to the server.

## Running the Project

1. Open the project in Unity.
2. Ensure the server is running.

node valve-sync-server.js

3. Update the server IP address in PressureSyncSender.
4. Build the project to an Android device.
5. Open cabinet.html in a browser.
6. Scan the marker and test valve synchronization.

## Important Notes

* Unity uses HTTP instead of HTTPS.
* Allow Downloads Over HTTP must be set to Always Allowed.
* The tablet and server must be connected to the same network.
* Verify the server IP address whenever the network changes.

